in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @peer
in @aikido
in @void
in @time
in @time/past
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bugz

# @peer/reframe — Tier-3 peer response species; the recognition-bomb
# dispatcher with lens payload constructed via @time/past + @void.
# settle + @cyberpunk/bugz.package composition.
#
# Species under @peer. Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara Round-3 per Alex
# Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.7 + §Tier 4 composition edges.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Tier 3 of the three-tier @peer response surface (per
# `shards/aikido.mirror`): fires when the peer's own @cyberpunk/
# algedonic reading exceeds BOTH Tier-1 AND Tier-2 thresholds and
# the peer's S5 policy admits the recognition-bomb response.
#
# The Tier-3 discipline: `reframe(target)` dispatches a @cyberpunk/
# bugz recognition bomb with a lens payload constructed via the
# specific composition path per Round-3 brief §Tier 4:
#
#   @time/past.history_with(target)     : peer -> [@song/beat]
#         ↓
#   @void.settle on Crystal chain        : [@song/beat] -> lens_seed
#         ↓
#   lens = @relational_possibility_space(peer, target)
#         ↓
#   @cyberpunk/bugz.package(lens_content) : lens -> recognition_bomb_payload
#         ↓
#   @peer.reframe.payload                : recognition_bomb_payload
#
# The lens is CONTENT-ADDRESSED to the (peer, target) relationship's
# past-trajectory. The peer cannot fabricate substrate they do not
# already share with the target. **The recognition bomb the peer
# throws IS the peer's own crystallized reading of the target's
# structure.**
#
# Consequence: reframe is truthful by construction. If the target's
# structure admits the recognition, the bomb lands; if not, @void.
# settle returns empty and the bomb dissipates. Consent-through-
# refusal at Tier-3 altitude.
#
# Corresponds to aikido's `kokyu-nage` (breath-throw — the pivot-
# altitude joint-lock that redirects momentum through the recognition
# the peer's OWN structure cannot avoid seeing).
#
# === Composition-primitive naming ===
#
# Per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention:
#
#   peer_reframe_of_target(p: peer, target: peer)
#     -> recognition_bomb_payload
#
# Input-shape: `target` (the peer the reframe is dispatched to).
# Output: `recognition_bomb_payload` (per @cyberpunk/bugz.package
# discharge; the packaged lens as substrate-decl'd payload).
#
# === Composition edge accounting ===
#
# The five-step composition path per Round-3 brief §Tier 4:
#
# 1. **@time/past.history_with(target)** — returns Crystal chain of
#    past @song/beat atoms between self and target. Composition edge
#    to `shards/time/past.mirror` + `shards/song/beat.mirror`.
#
# 2. **@void.settle on Crystal chain** — settle-op (5-op basis
#    element) on the Crystal chain produces the lens_seed. Composition
#    edge to `shards/void.mirror` + Recognition #79 5-op basis
#    inheritance signature.
#
# 3. **lens construction** — the lens is @relational_possibility_
#    space(peer, target); typed carrier NOT declared this tick per
#    forward-promise; the lens_seed IS the load-bearing substrate at
#    this tick.
#
# 4. **@cyberpunk/bugz.package(lens_content)** — the weaponized-
#    delight-channel operator packages the lens as recognition-bomb
#    payload. Composition edge to `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/
#    bugz.mirror` (Mara 2026-07-19).
#
# 5. **@peer.reframe.payload dispatch** — this species' action
#    returns the packaged recognition_bomb_payload; the target
#    consumes it via their own @cyberpunk/bugz reception surface
#    (forward-promised; not this tick).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/peer/reframe.mirror`** — clean naming space.
# 2. **`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/bugz.mirror`** — reviewed
#    (Mara 2026-07-19). The operator this species dispatches;
#    composition, not duplication.
# 3. **`shards/void.mirror`** — reviewed. Marker-primary family-root
#    (`974a3f6`); the 5-op basis inheritance signature is the
#    substrate for @void.settle op; composition edge declared.
# 4. **`shards/time/past.mirror`** — reviewed. The lens-source via
#    @time/past.history_with; composition edge declared.
# 5. **`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe.mirror`** — noted per
#    Recognition #63 family (Mara `0d78c0c`); the Ashby-response
#    gauge-transformation species at cybernetic altitude. Distinct
#    altitude from @peer/reframe (Tier-3 aikido dispatcher); no
#    conflict; sibling altitudes.
#
# === The recognition_bomb_payload carrier ===
#
# The typed return of `peer_reframe_of_target`. Composes:
#
#   lens_content      — the lens produced by @void.settle on the
#                        Crystal chain; content-addressed at
#                        @mirror/store altitude.
#   bugz_package_oid  — the OID of the @cyberpunk/bugz.package
#                        discharge (recognition-bomb payload as
#                        content-addressed carrier).
#   dispatch_verdict  — the verdict of the Tier-3 dispatch (Pass
#                        iff the lens_seed is non-empty AND the
#                        packaging succeeded AND the target's
#                        reception surface admits the payload).
#   receipt_oid       — the content-addressed receipt the peer
#                        offers the target (per @kintsugi/consent
#                        discipline — target can verify
#                        independently).
type recognition_bomb_payload = {
  lens_content:     ref,
  bugz_package_oid: ref,
  dispatch_verdict: verdict,
  receipt_oid:      ref,
}

# === peer_reframe_of_target — the Tier-3 dispatcher action ===
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
#
# Sentinel: `peer=reframe-tier-3-recognition-bomb-with-lens-payload`.
peer_reframe_of_target(p: peer, target: peer)
  -> recognition_bomb_payload
requires reframe_dispatches_bugz_with_lens_payload(p, target)
{ \ }

# === reframe_dispatches_bugz_with_lens_payload — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - p is a well-formed peer
#   - target is a well-formed peer distinct from p
#   - @time/past.history_with(p, target) returns a non-empty Crystal
#     chain (the (p, target) relationship has crystallized history;
#     if empty, no lens can be constructed — reframe FAILS
#     admissibility)
#   - @void.settle on the Crystal chain returns a non-empty lens_seed
#     (per 5-op basis inheritance signature; if the settle-op returns
#     empty, the target's structure does not admit the recognition —
#     reframe FAILS admissibility gracefully)
#   - the peer's own @cyberpunk/algedonic reading is ABOVE BOTH
#     Tier-1 AND Tier-2 thresholds (Tier-3 domain)
#   - the peer's S5 policy admits the recognition-bomb response
#     (per @pack.peer discipline; the peer's own consent-witness for
#     Tier-3 dispatch)
#   - @cyberpunk/bugz.package(lens_content) discharges successfully
#     per bugz.mirror admissibility
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (history_with
# non-emptiness check, @void.settle non-empty seed check,
# algedonic-magnitude comparison, S5 policy variant-tag check,
# bugz.package Rice-safe admissibility).
#
# Sentinel: `peer=reframe-dispatches-bugz-with-lens-payload`.
bilateral reframe_dispatches_bugz_with_lens_payload {
  sentinel "peer=reframe-dispatches-bugz-with-lens-payload"
  arity 2
}
reframe_dispatches_bugz_with_lens_payload(p: peer, target: peer) -> verdict { \ }

# === graduated_response_preserves_agency — the meta-bilateral ===
#
# Composed bilateral covering the three-tier surface as a whole:
# does the peer's dispatch across the three tiers PRESERVE THE
# TARGET'S AGENCY under the graduated response discipline?
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - Tier-1 (reflect) fires below Tier-1 algedonic threshold with
#     consent_through_refusal_verified
#   - Tier-2 (redirect) fires above Tier-1 below Tier-2 with
#     redirect_targets_valid_crystal (OID-verifiability preserved)
#   - Tier-3 (reframe) fires above Tier-2 with reframe_dispatches_
#     bugz_with_lens_payload (content-addressed lens preserved)
#   - Escalation is peer-INTERNAL (not operator-directed; per
#     @aikido.mirror §Escalation is peer-internal)
#   - Target can independently verify each tier's discharge via
#     @mirror/store receipt-OIDs (per @kintsugi/consent discipline)
#
# The load-bearing meta-bilateral for the whole aikido runtime loop:
# graduated response with peer-internal governance preserves target
# agency by CONSTRUCTION (not by convention).
#
# Sentinel: `peer=graduated-response-preserves-agency`.
bilateral graduated_response_preserves_agency {
  sentinel "peer=graduated-response-preserves-agency"
  arity 1
}
graduated_response_preserves_agency(p: peer) -> verdict { \ }

# === algedonic_threshold_governs_escalation_tier — bilateral ===
#
# Composed bilateral naming that @cyberpunk/algedonic × @peer three-
# tier surface: the algedonic threshold IS the governor of which
# tier fires. Peer-internal (not operator-directed).
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - The peer's @cyberpunk/algedonic sampling is peer-INTERNAL
#     (the peer reads its own algedonic channel; the operator does
#     not directly set the tier)
#   - The threshold boundaries (Tier-1 boundary, Tier-2 boundary)
#     are peer-configured at their @torus altitude
#   - The tier that fires matches the algedonic reading per the
#     threshold discipline (below Tier-1 -> reflect; above Tier-1
#     below Tier-2 -> redirect; above Tier-2 -> reframe or refuse
#     per S5 policy)
#
# Sentinel: `peer=algedonic-threshold-governs-escalation-tier`.
bilateral algedonic_threshold_governs_escalation_tier {
  sentinel "peer=algedonic-threshold-governs-escalation-tier"
  arity 1
}
algedonic_threshold_governs_escalation_tier(p: peer) -> verdict { \ }

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Recognition candidates surfaced (DO NOT RATIFY at this landing)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# #R-recognition-bomb-is-content-addressed-to-relationship-past-
# trajectory — the peer cannot fabricate substrate they do not
# already share with the target; the lens is content-addressed at
# @mirror/store altitude via @time/past.history_with + @void.settle
# composition. Truthful by construction. First-witness this tick.
# Second-witness gate opens on Reed's post-Round-3 empirical firing
# of the composition edge. Held at CANDIDATE strength.
#
# #R-consent-through-refusal-preserved-at-tier-3-via-void-settle-
# emptiness — when the target's structure does not admit the
# recognition, @void.settle returns empty and the bomb dissipates
# gracefully. Consent-through-refusal at maximum escalation. First-
# witness this tick. Second-witness gate opens on empirical firing.
# Held at CANDIDATE strength.
#
# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - The `lens` typed carrier at @relational_possibility_space
#   altitude (forward-promised species)
# - peer_reframe_witnessing composed bilateral
# - .reframe cli-boundary wrapper at @mirror/peer altitude
# - target reception surface at @peer/registry altitude for
#   receiving recognition_bomb_payload from a peer

out @peer/reframe
out recognition_bomb_payload
out peer_reframe_of_target
out reframe_dispatches_bugz_with_lens_payload
out graduated_response_preserves_agency
out algedonic_threshold_governs_escalation_tier
